gement and corporate advisory; it is 100% owned by AlRayan Bank, authorised by the QFC Regulatory Authority and regulated by the QFMA.","sourceIds":["S23","S26"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"IDENTITY","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null},{"claim":"Its stated purpose is to be the Gulf's leading Sharia-compliant asset manager and corporate advisory firm; its values are People, Trust, Excellence and Sharia.","sourceIds":["S23"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"PRIORITIES","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null},{"claim":"Asset management: public equities (Qatar and the Gulf), global sukuk and money markets; customised solutions for institutional and high-net-worth investors, with a focus on the GCC and Turkey. It manages the AlRayan GCC Fund and the AlRayan Qatar ETF (QATR).","sourceIds":["S23","S25"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"WHAT_THEY_DO","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null},{"claim":"Financial advisory: equity capital markets (IPOs, secondary offerings), debt capital markets (sukuk), M&A (buy-side and sell-side) and corporate finance (capital structure, restructuring).","sourceIds":["S24"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"WHAT_THEY_DO","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null},{"claim":"Its team page lists Akber Khan as Acting Chief Executive Officer, Zohaib Pervez as head of Asset Management (more than QAR5bn in client portfolios) and Hadi El Kadi as head of Financial Advisory.","sourceIds":["S27"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"ROLE","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null},{"claim":"Its site warns that entities are impersonating ARI, and says ARI has no lending licence.","sourceIds":["S23"],"evidenceClass":"VERIFIED","topic":"ARTICLE","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","asOf":null}],"sources":[{"sourceId":"S23","url":"https://www.alrayan.com/en/investment-banking","description":"AlRayan Investment official overview","publishedAt":null,"evidenceClass":"read 2026-10-11","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","excerpt":"Established in 2007 in Qatar, multi-award winning AlRayan Investment LLC (ARI) is a leading investment firm, focused on asset management and corporate advisory. … ARI is 100%-owned by AlRayan Bank (Masraf AlRayan QPSC). The firm is authorised by the QFC Regulatory Authority and regulated by the QFMA. … To be the Gulf’s leading Sharia-compliant asset manager and corporate advisory firm.","readAt":"2026-10-11","statusNote":"Official page read 2026-10-11."},{"sourceId":"S24","url":"https://www.alrayan.com/en/investment-banking/financial-advisory-group","description":"AlRayan Investment advisory services including capital markets and M&A","publishedAt":null,"evidenceClass":"read 2026-10-11","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","excerpt":"Equity Capital Markets advisory: IPOs, secondary offerings … Debt Capital Markets advisory: General debt advisory, sukuk issuance & Placement. … Buy-side and sell-side advisory services for local and cross-border transactions","readAt":"2026-10-11","statusNote":"Official page read 2026-10-11."},{"sourceId":"S25","url":"https://www.alrayan.com/investment-banking/asset-management-group/about-asset","description":"AlRayan Investment asset management and Sharia-compliant funds","publishedAt":null,"evidenceClass":"read 2026-10-11","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","excerpt":"AlRayan Investment provides customised investment solutions to institutional and High Net Worth investors … AlRayan Investment manages AlRayan GCC Fund, the largest mutual fund based in Qatar and the largest Sharia-compliant GCC fund in the world. … ARI manages AlRayan Qatar ETF (ticker QATR)","readAt":"2026-10-11","statusNote":"Official page read 2026-10-11."},{"sourceId":"S26","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/al-rayan-investment-llc/","description":"AlRayan Investment LinkedIn organization profile","publishedAt":null,"evidenceClass":"read 2026-10-11","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","excerpt":"Established in 2007 in Qatar, multi-award winning Al Rayan Investment LLC (ARI) is a leading investment firm … Specialties Asset Management and Corporate Financial Advisory","readAt":"2026-10-11","statusNote":"Official LinkedIn company page read 2026-10-11."},{"sourceId":"S27","url":"https://www.alrayan.com/investment-banking/team","description":"AlRayan Investment current public team page; roles can change","publishedAt":null,"evidenceClass":"read 2026-10-11","status":"VERIFIED_AGAINST_SOURCE","excerpt":"Akber is the Acting Chief Executive Officer of AlRayan Investment (ARI), bringing over 25 years of experience in the investment industry. … Zohaib has over 20 years of experience in the investment management industry. He joined ARI in 2015 and heads Asset Management. … Hadi joined ARI in 2019 and heads the Financial Advisory department.","readAt":"2026-10-11","statusNote":"Official team page read 2026-10-11."}],"quotes":[{"text":"To be the Gulf’s leading Sharia-compliant asset manager and corporate advisory firm.","sourceId":"S23","speaker":"AlRayan Investment LLC","date":null,"use":"SOURCE_QUOTE_ONLY"}],"profile":{"seedVersion":"1.1","verifiedAt":"2026-10-11","oneLine":"Qatar investment and advisory firm owned by AlRayan Bank, covering asset management, sukuk and M&A advisory.","summary":"AlRayan Investment (ARI) is a Qatar investment and advisory firm set up in 2007 and wholly owned by AlRayan Bank. Its asset management arm runs Sharia-compliant equity, sukuk and money-market strategies, including the AlRayan GCC Fund and the QATR ETF. Its advisory arm covers IPOs, sukuk, M&A and corporate finance. It is a firm to pitch Sharia-compliant financing or advisory, not a venture fund.","rehearsal":[{"topic":"Sharia-compliant financial structures","question":"How does your proposed investment meet Sharia requirements?","basisSourceIds":["S23"]},{"topic":"equity/debt and sukuk financing","question":"Why is the proposed financing route, equity or sukuk, appropriate?","basisSourceIds":["S24"]},{"topic":"corporate valuation and governance","question":"What valuation, financial statements and downside protections support this transaction?","basisSourceIds":["S24"]},{"topic":"financial advisory","question":"What advisory or partnership support are you actually seeking?","basisSourceIds":["S24"]}],"rehearsalTopics":["Sharia-compliant financial structures","equity/debt and sukuk financing","corporate valuation and governance","financial advisory"],"rehearsalQuestions":["How does your proposed investment meet Sharia requirements?","Why is the proposed financing route, equity or sukuk, appropriate?","What valuation, financial statements and downside protections support this transaction?","What advisory or partnership support are you actually seeking?"],"verification":[{"ordinal":0,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null},{"ordinal":1,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null},{"ordinal":2,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null},{"ordinal":3,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null},{"ordinal":4,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null},{"ordinal":5,"status":"VERIFIED","checkedAt":"2026-10-11","basis":"Stated on a page read on 2026-10-11; the excerpt is stored with the source.","note":null}],"contradicted":[],"quoteLabels":["from its own About page (stated purpose)"],"arabicNames":[{"text":"الريان للاستثمار","sourceId":"S27"}]}}]$j$::jsonb;
  e jsonb; s jsonb; f jsonb; pid uuid; ord integer;
begin
  for e in select * from jsonb_array_elements(doc) loop
    select id into pid from q_runtime.external_persons
     where profile_key = e->>'profileKey' and tenant_id is null;
    if pid is null then continue; end if;
    update q_runtime.external_persons
       set quotes = e->'quotes',
           profile = profile || (e->'profile'),
           last_researched_at = (e->>'lastResearchedAt')::timestamptz,
           updated_at = clock_timestamp()
     where id = pid;
    for s in select * from jsonb_array_elements(e->'sources') loop
      insert into q_runtime.external_entity_sources
        (external_person_id, source_id, url, description, published_at,
         evidence_class, status, excerpt, read_at, status_note)
      values (pid, s->>'sourceId', s->>'url', s->>'description', null,
              s->>'evidenceClass', s->>'status', s->>'excerpt',
              (s->>'readAt')::timestamptz, s->>'statusNote')
      on conflict (external_person_id, source_id) do update set
        url = excluded.url, description = excluded.description,
        evidence_class = excluded.evidence_class, status = excluded.status,
        excerpt = excluded.excerpt, read_at = excluded.read_at,
        status_note = excluded.status_note;
    end loop;
    ord := 0;
    for f in select * from jsonb_array_elements(e->'facts') loop
      insert into q_runtime.external_entity_facts
        (external_person_id, ordinal, claim, source_ids, evidence_class, topic, status, as_of)
      values (pid, ord, f->>'claim',
              array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(f->'sourceIds')),
              f->>'evidenceClass', f->>'topic', f->>'status', f->>'asOf')
      on conflict (external_person_id, ordinal) do update set
        claim = excluded.claim, source_ids = excluded.source_ids,
        evidence_class = excluded.evidence_class, topic = excluded.topic,
        status = excluded.status, as_of = excluded.as_of;
      ord := ord + 1;
    end loop;
  end loop;
end
$m$;
